0..69 Comment "// Each handler below answers an `extern` block\'s interface in gandr."
70..138 Comment "// The checker refuses each one where it leaves the block\'s members."
139..141 Comment "//"
142..217 Comment "// A clause answers a member that the block declares. It binds the member\'s"
218..296 Comment "// arguments as one payload, or none for a member of no argument, and then the"
297..367 Comment "// resumption. Each argument keeps its fixed-width type in the clause."
368..370 Comment "//"
371..444 Comment "// The first handler answers `sub`, which the block does not declare. The"
445..521 Comment "// second binds only the resumption of `add`, which takes two arguments. The"
522..573 Comment "// third sums the two `u32` arguments as `Integer`."
574..576 Comment "//"
577..655 Comment "// - see: `model/interop/boundary/round-trip.gandr` — a handler that answers"
656..679 Comment "//   the block in gandr"
681..755 Comment "// The boundary check reads `admitBlock` here, whatever the listing names."
